			"47": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SIZE\n\nSize is a very simple node; it gives you the size of a collection at attribute flow.\nThis node is mostly used to feed into other nodes that have a Size inlet to make sure that as the size of the collection goes up, so does the rest of the patch.\n\nIn this example we have an \"Amount\" slider that dictates how large the Linear nodes are and therefore how many circles we end up with. \nLater in the patch we want to colorize the circles using a Linear node. But we want to be sure we have colors equal to the amount of circles.\nSo we use the Size node and connect it to the size inlet on the Linear node.\n\nNote that we could just as well have dragged the \"Amount\" output to the Linear node, but as you might imagine, this would be very messy in larger patches.\n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 779.6160888671875,
					"width": 2138.9501953125,
					"x": -304.456207275390625,
